From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:42:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t7001-air2: Enable I2C1

I2C1 carries the iPad Air 2's two speaker amplifiers (MAX98721, at 0x31
and 0x34 in Apple's device tree). Enable the bus without clients so the
amplifiers can be identified from user space before a codec driver is
written.

Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
index d4b114f73..6f7db2f1c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
@@ -174,6 +174,15 @@ rtc_offset: rtc-offset@4 {
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * Speaker amplifiers (two MAX98721, at 0x31 and 0x34 in Apple's device
+ * tree). No driver binds them yet; the bus is enabled so they can be
+ * identified from user space.
+ */
+&i2c1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &serial5 {
 	pinctrl-0 = <&uart5_pins>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
